# CVE log

Audit findings and what was decided. Current state: `pnpm audit`.
Transitive pins are raised via `pnpm.overrides` in `package.json`.

## Open

**CVE-2026-14257** / GHSA-mh99-v99m-4gvg — brace-expansion, high, OOM DoS.
Present as 1.1.16 (`eslint>minimatch`) and 2.1.2 (`jest>@jest/core>@jest/reporters>glob>minimatch`).

Accepted. Fixed only in 5.0.8; the 1.x and 2.x lines have no backport and are already at their latest. v5 exports `{ expand }` rather than a callable, so an override breaks `minimatch`, which calls it as a function — verified: pinning it makes `eslint .` throw `TypeError: Error while loading rule 'react/display-name'`. Both paths are dev-only, reached only by glob matching over local file paths — no runtime exposure. Revisit when `minimatch` moves to a v5-compatible release.

## 2026-07-26 — added `@content-collections/cli`

No new findings. Added as a devDependency so `pnpm typecheck` can generate the
collections itself; audit unchanged at the two accepted paths above.

